			"notes": "# Structure DFU Cache 1.0.0\n\nInitial public release for Minecraft 1.21.1 on NeoForge.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Drop-in operation with no configuration or integration API.\n- Resolves the effective data-pack structure set during startup or an explicit `/reload`.\n- Uses Minecraft's official `DataFixTypes.STRUCTURE` and the exact `DataFixer` owned by `StructureTemplateManager`.\n- Stores passthrough and converted structure bytes in a persistent content-addressed cache.\n- Gives normal gameplay a complete single-layer vanilla structure resource pack with no mod tick hook, background cache worker, or runtime DFU job.\n- Falls back to the complete original resource manager if a generation cannot be prepared atomically.\n- Cache identity includes Minecraft, NeoForge, target DataVersion, and cache format.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1\n- NeoForge 21.1.248 through the 21.1.x line\n- Java 21\n\n## Validation\n\n- 11 focused tests passed with no failures, errors, or skips.\n- Minimal NeoForge 21.1.248 dedicated-server startup prepared 1,180 effective structure resources with zero vanilla fallbacks before reaching `Done`."
		}
